BEGIN_TEXT
When each of your nets meets: its name, the days, the start time (Zulu),
how long it runs, the channel by its plan label, net control and the
roster. You set all of it here; nothing about the schedule is kept from
you.

A sitting opens on time with its roster, on its own channel. While it is
open, a station heard on that channel is checked in by itself. A station
heard on another channel, after the sitting ends, or a station of the
amateur world is never checked in.

The schedule names channels, never frequencies. What a label stands for
is kept in the station's private channel plan.
END
BEGIN_EXAMPLE
A net that meets Tuesdays at 0100Z for 60 minutes on channel QXA, with
three stations on its roster. At 0100Z the sitting opens; STA-B is heard
on QXA at 0104Z and checked in.
END
